rt but they'd broken up  when moat was in jail for assault and he  was recently released  from durham prison in fact released from  durham  on thursday well detectives i remember  thinking  that samantha starbart must have been  absolutely terrified  raul mode had been crouching under the  living room window  as they came out of the house he opened  fire  and shot her boyfriend chris brown now  she  ran back into the house but you could  see from  the ground floor window into the lounge  he had shot  through that window hitting  samantha stubbart as she tried to take  cover  she is currently in hospital in a pretty  bad condition but police have told us  she will survive and they are at payne's  shots forward now  uh they're telling the public that they  would put in  a call to northumbria police  to say that he was going to shoot  police officers and what i'm talking  about is to tell you exactly why i've  done what i've done  [ __ ] the value is i'm not coming in the  line you just passed with me for  i mean i'll tell 20 this raumote had  promised not to stop until he was dead  and then in the early hours of sunday  that  investigation really escalated an  officer was shot in the early hours of  this morning he was carrying out a  static patrol  on a roundabout we understood  at porsche's one in the morning i got a  phone call  which was the worst phone call  of my professional life he was shot  through the windscreen  uh into the face and chest he's now in  hospital in a critical  but stable condition he has ten and a  half years david rathband was sitting  waiting and hoping to actually stop  raul moat and he'd been sitting  at a roundabout on the a1 a69  junction i looked to my left  through the the um  front passenger side of my police car  and i saw  mulch money from the a1 he lifted the  gun pushed it forward  and then discharged the weapon through  my my window  i felt all the pain and it was the  the shotgun um cartridge going through  my eye socket between my two eyes  round oats had gone up to him  and had callously shot him in the head  which resulted in in david being blinded  we are absolutely committed to finding  the man who did this  and are using every resource available  to bring this to a conclusion as quickly  as possible  nobody really knew what this man was  going to do  next  we had a gunman on the run the man  we are looking for is raul thomas  moat a very good morning to you welcome  to sunrise on monday the 5th of july our  top story  gunman on the run for the whole of  monday  the 5th of july into the tuesday  my focus was that crime scene at  berkeley we're live at the scene of one  of the shootings this is police  friends i remember police putting out  some detail  on a black lexus car that they thought  moat was using  we're live from rothbury and  northumberland where britain's both  now police found this black lexus at  rothbury  and immediately set up this huge  exclusion zone  around the town and i got straight into  the car  and started heading north detective  leading the hunt  for rao motor warned that the suspected  killer has  made threats against the public now  contradicting their earlier theory that  he  only posed to danger to police here this  massive  well my biggest fears of course  and my first objective was  to make sure that he was detained  and brought to justice before a court  for his crimes  and that was the one thing that i wanted  as well as  keeping the community and the police  officers safe  we knew that he had gone to ground in  rothbury what i was concerned about  was the fact that we were unable to  locate him  rothbury is in northumberland  and where moat was  is one of the most densely wooded  and least populated  parts of northumberland  i think at that point it felt like  the police were assembling a small army  if you like  in the most unlikely of places  there were reinforcements coming in from  all over the country  250 of them were armed and  they'd set up 