s the riverbank area in  the town  one of the community officers had gone  down to the riverbank and have actually  seen  raul mode and had called the firearms in  to surround him and to start negotiating  with him i wasn't aware of that at that  time  i had left rothbury just  after six o'clock  and as we got down to the a1 the  assistant chief constable  called me and said sue we've got him  surrounded  on the riverbank and there is a  negotiation going on between  the two parties ralmot on one side  carrying his uh  a weapon to his throat and the police on  the other side  this was the moment everything had been  building towards  some officers were taking cover behind  armored vehicles there were snipers with  rifles  some of them were literally standing in  the river  using anywhere to try and get a site of  moat  it's seven days since moat allegedly  shot and wounded  his former girlfriend samantha stobart  and killed her new partner  chris brown they thought raul moat was  going to kill  again and they were throwing everything  at it to try and stop him negotiations  between police  and moat are continuing moat has been  given food and water  and is eating and so i headed straight  into  the headquarters into the gold command  and i stayed there  my sole objective  was to capture ralmate  and to push him before a court it has  now been confirmed that the  footballer paul gascoigne has arrived  uh claiming to be a friend of ralmotz  and bring it with you there was this  kind of jaw-dropping moment paul  gascoigne  gaza one of britain's best-known  footballers  turned up at the cordon wanting to talk  to moat  wanting to help the situation but the  police  would not entertain the idea uh a  friendly face if you like  for uh uh this man rail mode paul  gascoigne the footballer apparently  as the night wore on no one really knew  how long this standoff was going to last  so i made my way back to one of the  local hotels that we've been put up in  what's happening kay is that police are  talking to ralph mort  covering him i turned on the television  and there's my colleague james matthews  reporting from the scene at the cordon  what you're looking at  are armed officers there's something and  you can see the silhouettes of the armed  officers moving around  with the green and grainy shots filmed  from our night vision camera  then there's what sounds like a shot  bear with me a second james matthews  with us james the latest  yeah okay i'm gonna hold the microphone  in the air we've just had a shot  i was sat in the gold command thing  and all of a sudden the call  came out shocked fired  and for a split second do you think  who shot who who shot who  [Music]  and it became clear very very quickly  that real mate had shot himself  and the ambulance was down there they  took him to the  hospital where he was declared dead  had shot himself at 12 minutes past one  in the morning  on july the 10th a post-mortem  examination  carried out the day after found that he  died from a shot  from his sworn-off shotgun  it was certainly one of the most  troubling  stories i've covered in my career  i've reported on a lot of murders  a lot of shootings but with this case it  was  so hard to predict where it was going to  go next and  in that scenario it meant who might be  killed next i live with the outcome i  live with the fact  we couldn't bring him to justice for the  families  of the people that he'd hurt  would like to give as i did at the time  my condolences to the family  of chris brown  to kath russband and the children of  david rathband for his  terrible death following  this incident and to some stubborn  for the injuries that she had they were  also  the innocent victims of this man  [Music]  sadly pc david rathband never recovered  from his injuries  he died by suicide in february 2012.  for more on this documentary go to  www.skynews.com  forward slash storycast 21.  the hunt for ral moat was written and  produced by robert mulhern  recordings research and production from  tom gillespie  next time i think i was like a boxer and  it doesn't  know whether i will be knocked out or he  will win by  points or in vienna as a kenyan athlete  attempts the impossible four-time london  marathon winner eliot kipchoge  hoping to become the first person in  history to run a marathon  in under two hours

